## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of streaming data structures, heap-based algorithms, and amortized complexity analysis in a real-time processing context.

## Key Concepts
- **Two-heap streaming median:** A max-heap stores the lower half; a min-heap stores the upper half.
- **Rebalancing invariant:** Heap sizes differ by at most one, ensuring the median is accessible in O(1).
- **Time complexity:** O(log n) per element for insertion plus O(log n) for rebalancing.
- **Space complexity:** O(n), proportional to total elements seen.

## Code Example
```javascript
insert(x) {
  if (L.isEmpty() || x <= L.max()) {
    L.insert(x);
  } else {
    R.insert(x);
  }
  rebalance();
}

rebalance() {
  if (L.size() > R.size() + 1) {
    R.insert(L.extractMax());
  } else if (R.size() > L.size() + 1) {
    L.insert(R.extractMin());
  }
}

getMedian() {
  if (L.size() > R.size()) return L.max();
  if (R.size() > L.size()) return R.min();
  return (L.max() + R.min()) / 2;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical streaming analytics under fixed memory, focusing on real-time percentile estimation and how rebinding affects accuracy and cost.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming histograms, fixed memory, boundary recomputation, percentile estimation, amortized analysis.
- Trade-offs between K, R, and accuracy; cache-friendly bucket access.

## Code Example
```javascript
class Histogram85 {
  constructor(M, K) {
    this.M = M; this.K = K;
    this.bounds = Array.from({length: K}, (_,i)=> Math.floor((i+1)*M/K));
    this.counts = new Array(K).fill(0);
  }
  update(x){
    let bucket = Math.min(this.K-1, Math.floor(x/ (this.M/this.K)));
    this.counts[bucket]++;
  }
  total(){ return this.counts.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0); }
  percentile(p){ // p in [0,1]
    const total = this.total();
    const target = p * total;
    let acc = 0;
    for(let i=this.K-1; i>=0; i--){
      acc += this.counts[i];
      if(acc >= target) return this.bounds[i-1] !== undefined ? this.bounds[i-1] : this.M;
    }
    return this.M;
  }
}
```

